=== Overview ===
'''{{Pink|Snake}}''' is a game, present in high enough '''Abiphone XIII ''' and above models, that allows players to play the [[w:Snake (video game genre)|classic game]].
;Models
*{{Item|Abiphone XIII Jade}}
*{{Item|Abiphone XIII Sapphire}}
*{{Item|Abiphone XIV Orange}}
*{{Item|Abiphone XIV Purple}}
*{{Item|Abiphone XIV Black}}
*{{ID|Abiphone Flip: Dragon}}
*{{ID|Abiphone Flip: Nucleus}}
*{{ID|Abiphone Flip: Volcano}}
*{{ID|AⒷiphone}}

=== Gameplay ===
'''{{Pink|Snake}}''' games start with a snake head in the middle of the menu. The player can navigate the snake, causing it to move in all directions except diagonally. The aim is to make the snake consume the apples that appear in random slots. Each time an apple is eaten, the snake grows a longer body, each piece symbolising one point. The game ends when the snake crashes into either itself or the edge of the menu.

The player's top score is kept track of, and can be viewed in the '''Abiphone'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s main menu.

=== Interface ===
{{:Abiphones/UI/Snake}}

<!-- TIC TAC TOE -->

|-|Tic Tac Toe=
=== Overview ===
'''{{Pink|Tic Tac Toe}}''' is a game, present in '''Abiphone XIV''' and above models, that allows players to play the [[w:Tic-tac-toe|classic game]] against an unbeatable [[w:Artificial intelligence|AI]].
;Models
*{{Item|Abiphone XIV Orange}}
*{{Item|Abiphone XIV Purple}}
*{{Item|Abiphone XIV Black}}
*{{ID|Abiphone Flip: Dragon}}
*{{ID|Abiphone Flip: Nucleus}}
*{{ID|Abiphone Flip: Volcano}}
*{{ID|AⒷiphone}}

=== Gameplay ===
'''{{Pink|Tic Tac Toe}}''' games start in a 3 by 3 grid, with the AI being on the {{Red|Red}} team, and the player on the {{Green|Green}} team. When either player selects a block, it will change from {{Item|White Wool}} to wool of their team's color. The game ends when either the player or AI scores three blocks in a row, column or diagonal, or both teams draw.

Previous scores are kept track of, and can be viewed in the '''Abiphone'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s main menu. 

