== Tips ==
*Due to the delay by ringing, {{NPCSprite|Queen Mismyla}}'s contact can be used for easier item switching to a mining tool with {{stat|mining wisdom}}, giving more {{skill|mining}} experience when claiming a reward.
*While calling {{NPCSprite|Maddox the Slayer}} might seem slower than using {{Item|Maddox Batphone}}, it can be sped up by using the '''/call''' command, the '''{{Aqua|Speed Dial}}''' feature and/or '''{{ID|Rezar® Abicase}}'''.

== Trivia ==
*Currently, there are {{Green|85}} contacts that can be added, and the maximum contact slots is {{Green|92}}.
* {{NPCSprite|Kaus}} and {{NPCSprite|Rollim}} will continue to call the player even if they have completed their training.
* The message {{RawMctxt|&7[&b✆&7] This NPC has an allergy to electromagnetism. It's a rare condition that isn't catalogued yet by the medicine community...}} is a reference to the show [[fandom:breakingbad:Better Call Saul (TV series)|''Better Call Saul'']].
** Specifically, it references [[w:Electromagnetic hypersensitivity|a condition]] that [[fandom:breakingbad:Chuck McGill|Chuck McGill]], the protagonist's brother, claims to have.
* Currently, there is no purpose of Maximum Discs, as [[Music Discs]] cannot be played with an '''Abiphone'''.
** {{NPCSprite|Udel}} mentioned the absence of the function in {{Aqua|Udel's Abiphone Keynote}}: "{{RawMctxt|&7&oIt would be better if they were playable...}}"
* According to {{NPCSprite|Tomioka}}'s dialogue, their great-grandfather invented the '''Abiphone'''.
* It used to be possible to put a [[Power Scroll]] on an '''Abiphone'''. Upon using the '''Abiphone''', the effect is given upon opening the menu, with the same cooldown applying to the effect as if it were any other right-click item.
**This could be used to apply its effects, such as using it before a fight for added {{Statname|Str}} or {{Statname|TD}} when facing tougher mobs or {{Statname|Mining Speed}} when mining.
** This has since been patched and is no longer possible. however, Abiphones that already had a [[Power Scroll]] applied still keep it.
* {{NPCSprite|Alixer}} is an '''Abiphone''' contact exclusive for {{gamemode|bingo}} profiles, which does not grant [[SkyBlock XP]]. It is unknown whether it would grant [[Accessory Power]], as [[Abicases]] are unobtainable on Bingo.
* {{NPCSprite|Udel}} used to sell '''Abiphones''' at {{Green|98.5%}} of their base prices, while {{NPCSprite|Nuvian}} sold them at {{Green|101.5%}} of their base prices.
* Prior to 0.23.4, lower-tiered '''Abiphones''' could be traded in to reduce the {{c|}} cost on the next tier.
* Despite some NPCs being located in [[The Catacombs]], there is no reception inside dungeons, so even NPCs like {{NPCSprite|Duncan}} cannot be reached from within them.

